Task 1.2 – Repair the Design (3 Marks)
Algorithm: Fractional Knapsack – LoadVehicle

Objective: Maximise the total value of packages loaded into a vehicle without exceeding its maximum weight capacity. Packages can be divided when necessary.

Greedy-choice rule: Always select the available package with the highest value-to-weight ratio first.

Pseudocode

text
ALGORITHM LoadVehicle

BEGIN

    READ N
    READ Capacity

    FOR i ← 1 TO N DO
        READ Weight[i]
        READ Value[i]

        Ratio[i] ← Value[i] / Weight[i]
    END FOR

    SORT all packages in descending order of Ratio

    RemainingCapacity ← Capacity
    TotalValue ← 0

    FOR i ← 1 TO N DO

        IF RemainingCapacity = 0 THEN
            EXIT FOR
        END IF

        IF Weight[i] <= RemainingCapacity THEN

            LoadedWeight[i] ← Weight[i]

            TotalValue ← TotalValue + Value[i]

            RemainingCapacity ← RemainingCapacity - Weight[i]

        ELSE

            LoadedWeight[i] ← RemainingCapacity

            TotalValue ← TotalValue +
                         (LoadedWeight[i] / Weight[i]) * Value[i]

            RemainingCapacity ← 0

            EXIT FOR

        END IF

    END FOR

    WRITE LoadedWeight
    WRITE TotalValue
    WRITE RemainingCapacity

    RETURN TotalValue

END ALGORITHM
Explanation of the Greedy Logic
Read the number of packages, vehicle capacity, package weights and values.

Calculate the value-to-weight ratio for every package.

Arrange packages in descending order of their ratios.

Select the package with the highest ratio first.

If the package fits completely, load it and update the remaining capacity and total value.

If the package does not fit completely, load only the fraction that fits.

Stop when the vehicle is full or all packages have been considered.

Return the maximum total value obtained.

