Task 1.3 – Design Defence (1 Mark)
The rewritten solution qualifies as pseudocode because it uses structured, language-independent statements such as READ, IF, FOR, SORT and RETURN to describe the algorithm. It clearly defines inputs, processing steps, decision conditions and outputs. It does not depend on the syntax or rules of any specific programming language. It is more precise than informal English because each operation and condition is explicitly stated, allowing another engineer to understand and implement the algorithm consistently.

Conclusion: The repaired algorithm uses the greedy approach to solve the Fractional Knapsack Problem. By selecting packages according to the highest value-to-weight ratio and allowing partial loading, it maximises the total value without exceeding vehicle capacity.


